HST Office: without the Windows Symbol font (Linux), Symbol text such as the pieces of the long
arrows in MathType equations was drawn with OpenSymbol, whose pieces do not join ("– –→").
The metric-compatible URW "Standard Symbols PS" (Debian/Ubuntu fonts-urw-base35, a dependency of
the HST .deb) is now the first substitute for Symbol, and symbol-encoded text (U+F0xx) is recoded
to its codes; OpenSymbol stays the fallback. Windows and macOS have Symbol and are unaffected.

